  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/...\nIssued 329 AM MDT MON APR 20 2026\nBreezy conditions and scattered showers will linger through \nThursday while the area remains influenced by a departing upper\nlow. Below- normal temperatures will also continue, with snow \nlevels holding between 4500-6000 ft MSL. On Friday, this upper \nlow will merge with a stalled Canadian trough over the northern \nU.S., reinforcing cool, northerly flow over the PacNW through \nthe weekend. While instability remains, diminishing moisture \nwill limit shower chances to 10-30% Friday-Sunday. Shower \nchances will primarily favor the higher terrain of SW Idaho, \nwith 4500-6500 ft snow levels. By Monday, the Canadian trough \nwill eventually shift east as weak ridging builds, resulting in \nmostly dry, slightly warmer conditions across SE Oregon and SW \nIdaho.",
